-- title:
--   The centralizer algebra of a cyclic multiplication operator
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $A$ be commutative semirings, with $A$ an $R$-algebra, and let $x\in A$. Suppose polynomial evaluation at $x$ is surjective:
--   $$R[t]\longrightarrow A,\qquad q\longmapsto q(x).$$
--   Write $L_a$ for multiplication by $a$ on the $R$-module $A$, and let
--   $$C_x=\{T\in\operatorname{End}_R(A):L_xT=TL_x\}$$
--   be its centralizer subalgebra, with multiplication given by composition.
--
--   There is a unique $R$-algebra isomorphism $e:A\simeq C_x$ satisfying
--   $$e(a)=L_a\qquad\text{for every }a\in A,$$
--   where the equality is taken in $\operatorname{End}_R(A)$ after inclusion of the centralizer.
--
--   No field, nontriviality, finite-dimensionality, or specified polynomial-kernel hypothesis is required.
-- source:
--   Derived supporting algebra lemma for the Senthil Kumar mission, reusing the proved polynomial_cyclic_commutant theorem (a572f240-2d39-4863-9c86-3b965e40549b). For a commutative R-algebra generated by one element x, its regular representation is a unique R-algebra equivalence onto the centralizer of multiplication by x. The map is injective by evaluation at 1 and surjective by the cyclic-commutant lemma. R and A may be arbitrary commutative semirings, including trivial ones; no field or finite-dimensionality assumption is needed. This is inferred supporting algebra, not a separately quoted theorem of the source article. At Mathlib revision 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474, AlgHom.codRestrict and Subalgebra.centralizer are in Algebra/Algebra/Subalgebra/Basic.lean, and AlgEquiv.ofBijective is in Algebra/Algebra/Equiv.lean. Primary documentation: https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Algebra/Subalgebra/Basic.html and https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Algebra/Equiv.html . No new definitions.

import Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.AlgebraMap
import Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Bilinear
import Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Subalgebra.Basic

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.polynomial_cyclic_centralizer_algebra
    (R A : Type*) [CommSemiring R] [CommSemiring A] [Algebra R A]
    (x : A)
    (hx : Function.Surjective (fun q : Polynomial R => q.eval₂ (algebraMap R A) x)) :
    ∃! e : A ≃ₐ[R] Subalgebra.centralizer R
        ({Algebra.lmul R A x} : Set (Module.End R A)),
      ∀ a : A, (e a : Module.End R A) = Algebra.lmul R A a := by sorry
